BT /F1 10 Tf 12 TL 56 760 Td (Inhalerbuddy) Tj T* () Tj T* (Executive Summary: Inhalerbuddy LLC) Tj T* () Tj T* (Overview) Tj T* () Tj T* (Inhalerbuddy is a connected health startup that is passionate about changing the way that) Tj T* (families, schools and pharmacies think about childhood asthma. We are a team of three students) Tj T* (at our university and we have formed an LLC and built a working prototype. This executive) Tj T* (summary will describe the problem, our solution, the market, our business model, the) Tj T* (competition, our team, our milestones and what we are asking for.) Tj T* () Tj T* (The Problem) Tj T* () Tj T* (Asthma is a very common condition among children and it is a problem that effects millions of) Tj T* (families. Many kids with asthma do not take there medicine the way that the doctor said, and) Tj T* (parents often do not know when a inhaler was used or not used. Sometimes a child will use the) Tj T* (rescue inhaler a lot more then normal in the days before a attack, but nobody notices because) Tj T* (there is no good way to see the pattern. This can lead to emergency room visits, missed school) Tj T* (days, and stress for the whole family. We beleive that this is a big problem that is not being) Tj T* (solved well today and that technology can help. Parents are busy and they want peace of mind) Tj T* (about there child's health.) Tj T* () Tj T* (The Solution) Tj T* () Tj T* (Our solution is Inhalerbuddy, which is a end-to-end platform that leverages Internet of Things) Tj T* (sensing, mobile software and human pharmacist support to create a seamless asthma management) Tj T* (experience. It has three pieces.) Tj T* () Tj T* (First, the Inhalerbuddy cap. This is a small electronic cap that snaps on to the top of most) Tj T* (common inhalers. It has a sensor that detects when the inhaler is pressed and it sends the time) Tj T* (to the phone using wireless. The cap is lightweight and designed to be kid friendly with fun) Tj T* (colors.) Tj T* () Tj T* (Second, the Inhalerbuddy app. The app shows caregivers a dashboard of when the medicine was) Tj T* (used. If the rescue inhaler is used more often then usual, the app sends a alert to the) Tj T* (caregivers so they can check on the child, call the doctor or take other steps before symptoms) Tj T* (get worse. The app also has reminders for daily controller medicine.) Tj T* () Tj T* (Third, the pharmacist check-in service. Once in a while a pharmacist reviews the data and) Tj T* (checks in with the family by message or call to answer questions and make sure the child is) Tj T* (using the inhaler properly. We think this human touch is what makes us different and gives) Tj T* (parents trust.) Tj T* () Tj T* (Together these three pieces create a holistic solution that is proactive instead of reactive.) Tj T* () Tj T* (Market) Tj T* () Tj T* (The market for our product is very large. There are millions of children with asthma in the) Tj T* (United States alone and the market for digital health is growing very fast. If we capture even) Tj T* (a small percent of families with asthmatic children, this would be a very large business. We) Tj T* (also believe there are opportunities internationally and with other conditions besides asthma,) Tj T* (such as other respiratory conditions and chronic disease management. Our target customers are) Tj T* (parents of children with asthma, and secondarily schools, pediatricians and pharmacies. We have) Tj T* (not yet done a formal market study but we have talked to a few parents and friends who thought) Tj T* (the idea was good.) Tj T* () Tj T* (Business Model) Tj T* () Tj T* (We plan to make money in several ways, and we are still figuring out which will work best. One) Tj ET
endstream
