BT /F1 10 Tf 12 TL 56 760 Td (option is to sell the cap as a one time purchase to parents at a price of around thirty to) Tj T* (fifty dollars. Another option is a monthly subscription for the app and the pharmacist service,) Tj T* (maybe five to ten dollars a month. We could also partner with pharmacies, insurance companies) Tj T* (or health systems who might pay us to offer Inhalerbuddy to their patients or members. There is) Tj T* (also the possibility of selling anonymized data to researchers or pharmaceutical companies,) Tj T* (which could be very valuable. We think a mix of these revenue streams will make the business) Tj T* (sustainable. Pricing will be determined after we do more testing with customers.) Tj T* () Tj T* (Competition) Tj T* () Tj T* (There are some other companies that make smart inhaler sensors and asthma apps. However we feel) Tj T* (that our product is better because it combines hardware, software and a pharmacist service in) Tj T* (one package and because it is focused on kids and caregivers. Other products are mostly for) Tj T* (adults or for the patient only. Also, our design is more fun and friendly for children. We) Tj T* (believe that no competitor offers the full solution that we do, and we have a first mover) Tj T* (advantage in the pharmacist check-in piece. We will also build a strong brand which will be) Tj T* (hard to copy.) Tj T* () Tj T* (Team) Tj T* () Tj T* (Brandon Tilley is our CEO and he is a junior studying business. He is a natural leader and has) Tj T* (always been interested in health and entrepreneurship. Marisol Quenneville is our CTO and she) Tj T* (is a senior studying electrical engineering, and she designed and built the prototype cap.) Tj T* (Devraj Ostrowski is our head of product and he is a junior studying computer science, and he) Tj T* (built the first version of the app. Our team is hardworking, passionate and committed to making) Tj T* (Inhalerbuddy a success. We do not yet have a pharmacist or a clinician on the team but we plan) Tj T* (to find advisors, and one of our relatives is a nurse who has given us some feedback.) Tj T* () Tj T* (Milestones and Financials) Tj T* () Tj T* (So far we have reached two main milestones. We defined our core business concept and we built a) Tj T* (prototype of the cap and a early version of the app. We have also formed a LLC. The prototype) Tj T* (works in the lab and can detect when it is pressed and send the data to the phone, although the) Tj T* (battery life and the fit on different inhalers still needs work. We have not yet tested with) Tj T* (real patients or children and we have no customers or revenue at this time. We have also not) Tj T* (yet made a website. Our expenses so far have been small and paid for by the founders out of) Tj T* (pocket, mostly for electronic parts and a few app tools. Over the next year, we expect to need) Tj T* (money for manufacturing, regulatory work, app development, pharmacist staffing and marketing.) Tj T* (We think we could reach substantial revenue in about three years if things go well, though we) Tj T* (have not yet built a detailed financial model.) Tj T* () Tj T* (What We Are Asking For) Tj T* () Tj T* (We are applying to this competition for several reasons. First, we hope to win prize money) Tj T* (which we would use to improve the prototype and begin a small pilot. Second, we are looking for) Tj T* (mentorship from experienced entrepreneurs and healthcare professionals who can help us with our) Tj T* (business model and with navigating regulations. Third, we would like introductions to potential) Tj T* (partners such as pharmacies, pediatric clinics and schools. Finally we want feedback from the) Tj T* (judges on how to make our idea stronger. We are excited about the opportunity and we thank you) Tj T* (for considering our application. With your support we beleive Inhalerbuddy can make a real) Tj T* (difference in the lives of children with asthma and there families.) Tj ET
endstream
